[{:db/id "q-40382/selection/665a73a8c00dc5bd1f07c4b0b5cd2186eab140daadbd1232d59c6292fdf61286" :answer/id #uuid "e50ea77b-714b-59ae-9135-bb8319e2da92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40382/selection/e0ba402cd84d13c6f5cc302d688a40998a3c2db6031623902c95924bf47f6142" :answer/id #uuid "b07ae444-92c8-5bb3-a820-0d2f3620c7e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40382/selection/fc1450d3a68ce2470d2466f05a9599a2ca1a9cc197fbc9e198df52b137cd3145" :answer/id #uuid "52869a31-3335-5163-86d7-2e6dd36ae326" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40382/selection/bac48798b3820cd0c0ea624811962c312ad4120767a3184feb4e4b8736ace894" :answer/id #uuid "4beb1a26-d16d-5753-8849-8e1f2f8fe7b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40382/selection/f054999c7d0210e6bb734b791e16302328bc00519b26da2abc32d3049fc540da" :answer/id #uuid "67e362ec-f183-550d-ba98-3c40833e2745" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$-" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40382/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5334d272-a1c7-5e85-8d98-e81f7bea668b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-40382/selection/bac48798b3820cd0c0ea624811962c312ad4120767a3184feb4e4b8736ace894" :answer-field/choices ["q-40382/selection/665a73a8c00dc5bd1f07c4b0b5cd2186eab140daadbd1232d59c6292fdf61286" "q-40382/selection/e0ba402cd84d13c6f5cc302d688a40998a3c2db6031623902c95924bf47f6142" "q-40382/selection/fc1450d3a68ce2470d2466f05a9599a2ca1a9cc197fbc9e198df52b137cd3145" "q-40382/selection/bac48798b3820cd0c0ea624811962c312ad4120767a3184feb4e4b8736ace894" "q-40382/selection/f054999c7d0210e6bb734b791e16302328bc00519b26da2abc32d3049fc540da"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-40382" :question/id #uuid "b4a044e4-626a-5104-b82d-85d02c9e27ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-40382" :question/problem "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $a=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].$ If $x=y+z,$ where $y\\in \\text{Span}{a}$ and $z⊥\\text{Span}{a},$ then $z=$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/assets/d887852fe51f08cb7296437e69b6a9632721cfd155558e6abf9a99b4f59f7ad6.png)\n\nFirst, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{a}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x & =\\frac{a\\cdot x}{a\\cdot a}a \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\cdot 5+3\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot (-1)+6\\cdot 4}{{6}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{6}^{2}}a \\\\  & =\\frac{30+3+3+24}{36+9+9+36}a \\\\  & =\\frac{60}{90}a \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}a \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we get the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ z & =x-{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $y\\in \\text{Span}{a}$ and $z⊥\\text{Span}{a},$ as shown in the picture above.\n\nIn conclusion, $z=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-40382/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "144d1258-f8d5-55e9-be38-ec25b6f84bd3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40382"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-40411/selection/bb5e3e524771fed0f8298cd585cdb5759ed07bb1ac0ac034d00b73a0b668a9ce" :answer/id #uuid "83e968de-71e1-5552-9aa7-cdbc869add4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40411/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" :answer/id #uuid "417b0985-3ca6-5207-ad28-eb5bb1233a98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40411/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer/id #uuid "d5898af1-de52-59d0-88ba-bba8480474b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40411/selection/f00d8b7a5eeed0dcaa02b7f16c350647a90a461726a760f9ecdf0379dbf8fa63" :answer/id #uuid "af46196a-d3de-5456-a912-86d3600193d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40411/selection/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629" :answer/id #uuid "e7a0b0af-3318-57aa-86db-094ae9509e3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40411/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "61d3d751-590a-5102-b6c8-c119b8ebd679" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-40411/selection/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629" :answer-field/choices ["q-40411/selection/bb5e3e524771fed0f8298cd585cdb5759ed07bb1ac0ac034d00b73a0b668a9ce" "q-40411/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" "q-40411/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" "q-40411/selection/f00d8b7a5eeed0dcaa02b7f16c350647a90a461726a760f9ecdf0379dbf8fa63" "q-40411/selection/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-40411" :question/id #uuid "85dd34e8-2b5f-5859-8535-1eea4bd665a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-40411" :question/problem "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the distance between $x$ and $\\text{Span}{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "The distance between the vector $x$ and the vector space $\\text{Span}{b}$ is given by $‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖$, where $\\overset{^}{x}$ in the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{span}{b}.$\n\nFirst, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{b}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{b\\cdot x}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-2)+(-1)(-2)}{(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{-2-2-2+2}{1+1+1+1}b \\\\  & =-b \\\\  & =-1[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{((-2)-(-1))^{2}+(2-1)^{2}+((-2)-(-1))^{2}+((-2)-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+1+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{12} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-40411/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "144d1258-f8d5-55e9-be38-ec25b6f84bd3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40411"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81201/selection/756ce8b4ae45d34988d633ac59ba79bc54d283d37f6715daf221800245ab4d78" :answer/id #uuid "f5592fb0-7bda-5e77-a170-ce5b6d142bfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81201/selection/80f7643749639dc6ac3cb6ea590a80572731108334d6c4e6c17a301b44d6338a" :answer/id #uuid "7307b587-1304-5b08-a06f-7d20566c3f5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81201/selection/ba6503d90d6b572c9cc7470c7b48a7d345a0bf0c91ae0152e2b99638fe248548" :answer/id #uuid "8de28337-3c6b-5e6c-bc10-c47fb1d28ba3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81201/selection/51a095e0b68bf5e4f23f4ce05cd97d0463c784481999fd29715f89caae21911b" :answer/id #uuid "3e7837f6-fb26-5141-a4df-016c18dde3db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81201/selection/655ede254939c8720ff15fa47ebfaa58a37f5de0c0b757a45cc6bf14b9606903" :answer/id #uuid "dea93dda-0e87-56df-9088-82ca3fe128f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81201/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0e9c6ba3-3cd3-50eb-b42f-45c6274e8ca8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81201/selection/51a095e0b68bf5e4f23f4ce05cd97d0463c784481999fd29715f89caae21911b" :answer-field/choices ["q-81201/selection/756ce8b4ae45d34988d633ac59ba79bc54d283d37f6715daf221800245ab4d78" "q-81201/selection/80f7643749639dc6ac3cb6ea590a80572731108334d6c4e6c17a301b44d6338a" "q-81201/selection/ba6503d90d6b572c9cc7470c7b48a7d345a0bf0c91ae0152e2b99638fe248548" "q-81201/selection/51a095e0b68bf5e4f23f4ce05cd97d0463c784481999fd29715f89caae21911b" "q-81201/selection/655ede254939c8720ff15fa47ebfaa58a37f5de0c0b757a45cc6bf14b9606903"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81201" :question/id #uuid "cf6989c8-075d-5aa8-b8e4-69c49c524008" :question/math-academy-id "q-81201" :question/problem "Given the vector $x$ and the system of  linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=3{x}_{2}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot 1}{{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{10}b \\\\  & =b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-81201/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8d8c7fb-e69a-5b52-9566-4d2e0c7e54fc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81201"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140116/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer/id #uuid "ba78cf4d-7fef-5f4b-b02a-1a4b87b86919" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140116/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "2c2082e3-af24-5892-a064-1e7a7d991614" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140116/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" :answer/id #uuid "6f1a2acb-4ce6-516e-981b-4e1769dfc1bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140116/selection/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629" :answer/id #uuid "2f72a3a8-df5d-5ad4-85bc-476f487db85a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140116/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "806e4323-aba4-5ac3-bda1-13e6817aec35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140116/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a2f7c596-8e7b-5481-b2a1-311f2ea5d082" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140116/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-140116/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" "q-140116/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-140116/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" "q-140116/selection/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629" "q-140116/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140116" :question/id #uuid "570cf60f-9243-57d5-ac91-c6c37f3016fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-140116" :question/problem "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ Find the distance between $x$ and $\\text{Span}{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "The distance between the vector $x$ and the vector space $\\text{Span}{b}$ is given by $‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖$, where $\\overset{^}{x}$ in the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{span}{b}.$\n\nFirst, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{b}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{b\\cdot x}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 3+1\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot (-2)+0\\cdot (-2)}{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{6+4+2}{4+1+1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{6}b \\\\  & =2b \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3-4)^{2}+(4-2)^{2}+(-2-(-2))^{2}+(-2-0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4+0+4} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-140116/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "144d1258-f8d5-55e9-be38-ec25b6f84bd3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140116"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140118/selection/905ae8ee39048b9392c78f195eb6dfa97172546e65cfb5266a0bdd411c2676bf" :answer/id #uuid "41c24f26-a593-54e3-8e83-01777fe77391" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140118/selection/9576b88f964aafa72109b0daf8e5011e1276983566a81ec66c0ae1d06856933c" :answer/id #uuid "f52b5101-f703-56aa-99b0-3fb560561ddb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140118/selection/a98b3b253bfcf7abf8ec65fc3343a0885fc4195d7023a1cd8dafa18976576c14" :answer/id #uuid "65d11f9e-4b61-56d9-8790-1de18509d0ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140118/selection/a58e880e036264e5b21442a2e9867416c984cde73a96371bb168dcb66090a333" :answer/id #uuid "198c034a-d2a2-567a-89ae-5c014bf3d1d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140118/selection/58b8499b68d4ac9e42288a6c6a8876a0a4f47635267d19f2bcfe1ac12fac3171" :answer/id #uuid "d3b612fd-b7bf-581e-a13e-edecbb7e6afd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140118/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "39bee12b-bb96-5c7b-af71-fb205957ed40" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140118/selection/905ae8ee39048b9392c78f195eb6dfa97172546e65cfb5266a0bdd411c2676bf" :answer-field/choices ["q-140118/selection/905ae8ee39048b9392c78f195eb6dfa97172546e65cfb5266a0bdd411c2676bf" "q-140118/selection/9576b88f964aafa72109b0daf8e5011e1276983566a81ec66c0ae1d06856933c" "q-140118/selection/a98b3b253bfcf7abf8ec65fc3343a0885fc4195d7023a1cd8dafa18976576c14" "q-140118/selection/a58e880e036264e5b21442a2e9867416c984cde73a96371bb168dcb66090a333" "q-140118/selection/58b8499b68d4ac9e42288a6c6a8876a0a4f47635267d19f2bcfe1ac12fac3171"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140118" :question/id #uuid "61cc989f-9d11-52b3-b431-d0b4753db895" :question/math-academy-id "q-140118" :question/problem "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a basis for the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=-3{x}_{2}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{(-4)\\cdot (-3)+8\\cdot 1}{{(-3)}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{10}b \\\\  & =2b \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-140118/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8d8c7fb-e69a-5b52-9566-4d2e0c7e54fc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140118"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
